 "notes": [
  "Fastweb + Vodafone: Swisscom completed the Vodafone Italia deal on 2024-12-31. Vodafone Italia was legally merged into Fastweb S.p.A. on 2026-01-01 (Wikipedia), so the former Vodafone and Fastweb holdings are one operator here.",
  "3.4–3.6 GHz: AGCOM 201/24/CONS (June 2024) gave MIMIT a favourable opinion on the transfer of OpNet's (Brightco S.r.l.) 3.4–3.6 GHz and 24.5–26.5 GHz rights to WindTre. It is shown as completed because lteitaly.it lists the block as OpNet/WindTre. No MIMIT completion notice was found.",
  "Regional variants in 3.4–3.6 GHz (Bolzano, Valle d'Aosta) are described in the band note; the diagram shows the layout for the rest of Italy.",
  "2.3 GHz: the temporary local award (Feb 2026, to end-2029) is excluded from totals because it covers only six provinces.",
  "Defence/public-safety blocks (1800, 2600 FDD/TDD, 3.4–3.6 GHz) are shown as a government operator.",
  "Sanity check: iliad totals 2×45 MHz + 220 MHz excluding 2.3 GHz, matching its 2025 annual report."
